From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stateful-audio <stateful-audio@ffmpeg.devel>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 10:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] lavfi/af_amix: clamp input_state to INPUT_ON at
 ff_amix_set_state restore time

Phase 11 resolution: eliminates a stall in ff_amix_set_state when the
captured state snapshot reflects end-of-prior-segment semantics
(INPUT_EOF set on every input, INPUT_ON cleared because fifos drained).

Integration callers such as nginx-vod-module flush every buffersrc with
NULL when a source exhausts (audio_filter_choose_source), then capture
amix state after audio_encoder_flush. By that point amix's activate()
has observed status=EOF on every inlink, drained each fifo, and cleared
INPUT_ON per af_amix.c:481-483. Restoring that byte-for-byte onto a
freshly-configured graph causes calc_active_inputs() to return
AVERROR_EOF on the first activate() call -- the restored graph emits
zero output for the remainder of the segment.

The captured EOF bits describe transport-level source readiness at the
end of the PRIOR segment; on the RESUMED segment the sources are fresh
buffersrcs that have not yet reached EOF. scale_norm[], next_pts, and
frame_list remain meaningful DSP-level state. Only the input_state[]
EOF flags must be rewritten.

Library reproducer: test-harness/phase11_amix_repro.c in the
stateful-aac-validation repo. Pre-fix: chunks 1..3 emit 0 samples
(stall). Post-fix: all 4 chunks emit full CHUNK_FRAMES*FRAME_SIZE
samples (110592 each). bit_exact_amix --matrix remains 25/25 PASS.

Signed-off-by: stateful-audio <stateful-audio@ffmpeg.devel>
---
 libavfilter/af_amix.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

--- a/libavfilter/af_amix.c
+++ b/libavfilter/af_amix.c
@@ -1123,6 +1123,24 @@ int ff_amix_set_state(AVFilterContext *ctx, const uint8_t *buf, size_t size)
     /* pass 2: apply */
     ff_ffsa_reader_find(&r, FFSA_AMIX_INPUT_STATE, &val, &vlen);
     memcpy(s->input_state, val, (size_t)s->nb_inputs);
+
+    /* Phase 11 fix: when restoring amix state onto a freshly-configured
+     * graph (e.g. nginx-vod-module per-segment construction), the captured
+     * input_state reflects end-of-prior-segment semantics where sources
+     * have been flushed with EOF and their fifos drained. Restoring that
+     * byte-for-byte would leave INPUT_ON cleared across all inputs,
+     * causing activate() to observe active_inputs==0 and immediately
+     * emit AVERROR_EOF -- the restored graph produces zero output.
+     *
+     * The semantically correct behaviour is: on a resumed graph the
+     * inputs are fresh (new buffersrcs, no EOF yet), so we must clear
+     * INPUT_EOF and set INPUT_ON for every input. scale_norm[] /
+     * next_pts / frame_list contents are still meaningful state to carry
+     * forward; only the EOF flags need rewriting because they describe
+     * transport-level input readiness, not the mixer's internal DSP. */
+    for (i = 0; i < s->nb_inputs; i++) {
+        s->input_state[i] = INPUT_ON;
+    }
 
     ff_ffsa_reader_find(&r, FFSA_AMIX_SCALE_NORM, &val, &vlen);
     for (i = 0; i < s->nb_inputs; i++)
 